// spectral_split_rack_main.genexpr — template of the per-sample code of a Spectral Split device that shares ONE analysis per rack.
// scripts/spectral_common.py (expand_rack_core) splices the two sections below into a device core at its `//@SS_DECL` and `//@SS_MAIN`
// markers, substitutes the @@...@@ placeholders and moves the device's `//@hook <name>` blocks into the marked places.
// Written for src/transplit_core.genexpr (the reference device); Loud / Harmonic / Freq Split adopt it with the same contract.
//
// WHY. A device sits first in EVERY chain of an Audio Effect Rack and all instances see the identical input. Before this, each ran the
// whole analysis + STFT and kept one channel (K x the work), and each framed the signal at its own sample phase (instances started at
// different times, or a linked Size change reaching the peers 80-160 ms apart, gave different frames, so the chains no longer summed to the
// input). Measured in Live (VM, scripts/test_spectral_probe_live.js, AGENTS.md section 22): the chains of a rack are processed on DIFFERENT
// THREADS in blocks of the host buffer (512 samples = 8 vectors of 64), in no fixed order, so one instance's data is visible to another only
// after the block (the join) and reads inside the other's current block can be torn. The design therefore never relies on same-vector
// visibility: it exchanges data with a lag larger than a block.
//
// ROLES (set by the face through the messages role / serve / epoch / ring / lead, see src/spectral_link.js):
//   (role -1, the default) not told yet: the instance neither computes nor follows and outputs silence until the face sends its role (a deferred gen~
//                   starts before its messages arrive; starting as SELF would frame the signal at a phase unrelated to the leader's and break the rack sum).
//   SELF   (role 0) outside a rack: compute only the own output channel, exactly the pre-rack behaviour.
//   LEAD   (role 1) the one instance of a rack group that computes: frames the signal, analyses it once, and for every served output
//                   channel applies the channel's mask, inverse-transforms and overlap-adds. The outputs are written into the instance's own
//                   output RING at INPUT time (field 1.. of the slot of the input sample's counter), next to the input fingerprint (field 0).
//   FOLLOW (role 2) does not frame or analyse. It reads its channel from the leader's ring. All instances output the ring at INPUT time
//                   index (counter - LATENCY), which is why LATENCY must exceed (the largest STFT latency n - 1) + (the host block): 5120 here.
//                   If its leader data cannot be used (not aligned, leader gone, different input, ring underrun) it falls back to computing
//                   its own channel (SELF behaviour) and keeps doing so until the face sends a new epoch.
//   The leader writes the pure wet channel signals; Mix, the dry path, Output and the final gain are applied by every instance itself.
//
// SHARED SAMPLE CLOCK. Every instance counts its samples modulo 2^22. The offset D between the leader's counter and an instance's own counter is
// found by CONTENT: both write a fingerprint of the (bit-identical) input into their ring, and the follower finds the leader sample index whose
// fingerprint window equals its own (ss2_align), then re-verifies it at every vector (ss2_verify). No other clock exists inside a host that
// processes the chains concurrently, and the same check detects a follower whose input differs from the leader's (a device placed after
// another device): it then computes by itself. A late-started instance does not frame at all, so its hop phase cannot differ; a Size change
// happens only in the leader (followers never use their own Size); an instance that restarts re-finds D and plays from the ring again.
//
// GAPS. When the leader's pipeline restarts (first start, Size change, becoming leader) the output between the last complete old output and the
// first complete new one is invalid. The leader zeroes it, publishes its bounds (gapS, gapE) and every reader fades its output down before
// gapS and up after gapE by the READ index (the reader is more than 1000 samples ahead of the leader's write, so it knows in time).
//
// RING LAYOUT (buffer ---ssring, one per instance, 16 + RS * STRIDE floats). Header: 0 next output index to write (wTau), 1 fingerprint count
// (leader counter + 1 of the last completed vector), 2 gapS, 3 gapE, 4 computing flag, 5 served-channel mask, 6 n, 7 layout version, 8 LATENCY,
// 9 ring age in samples (saturating). Slot i (counter mod RS): field 0 fingerprint, field 1 + 2c / 2 + 2c = output row c left / right
// (c = 0..K-1 the channels, c = K the "All" mask row).
//
// DEVICE CONTRACT (what a core must add; transplit_core.genexpr is the example):
//   * functions first (device analysis), then `//@SS_DECL`, then its own Data / Param / History declarations (Buffer scope, the per-bin
//     state, its Params and History), then its control-refresh statements?  NO: control refresh is a hook, see below. Then `//@SS_MAIN`.
//   * Buffer scope(...) with the device's telemetry (the template writes the common scalars at @@SCB@@ + 0..17); Data ms(2049, 2) Mid
//     spectrum comes from the template; the device declares its mask Data (@@MKD@@) with the final masks of channel c in row @@MKB@@ + c
//     (c = 0..K-1) and the sum of all channels in row @@MKB@@ + K.
//   * `//@hook ctl` ... `//@endhook`: statements that copy Params into History every 32 samples (variables: n, sr, selH, mixH are set).
//   * `//@hook frame` ... `//@endhook`: statements run once per hop after ss_mid(): compute the masks. Variables: ms, n, sr, sAge (0 = state just
//     restarted, up to 3), the template advances sAge afterwards.
//   * `//@hook tele` ... `//@endhook`: statements run on telemetry frames (about every 1024 samples, awake) of the computing instance after
//     the masks exist: fill the device's columns of `scope`. (Followers' faces read the leader's scope.)
//   * Mix: the device's Param is called mixamt. outsel is 0 = All, 1..K = channel.
//
// GenExpr: see the rules at the top of spectral_split_rack.genexpr.

//@@SECTION decl
Buffer ring("ssring");
Buffer lead("sslead");
Data tab(4096, 3);
Data win(4096);
Data fx(4096, 2);
Data fy(4096, 2);
Data ringL(4096);
Data ringR(4096);
Data accD(4096, @@ACCROWS@@);
Data stt(8);
Data ms(2049, 2);
Data cols(512);
Data aw(64);
Data sFlag(8);
Delay dryL(@@LAT1@@);
Delay dryR(@@LAT1@@);

Param fftn(1024);
Param outsel(0);
Param mixamt(1);
Param role(-1);
Param serve(0);
Param epoch(0);

History sCnt(0);
History nCur(0);
History sCtl(0);
History sBoot(0);
History selH(0);
History roleH(-1);
History serveH(0);
History epH(0);
History epSeen(-1);
History mixH(1);
History mixS(1);
History mixInit(0);
History sOwnH(1);
History eserveH(1);
History cmpH(0);
History fbk(0);
History als(0);
History dOff(0);
History noMatch(0);
History staleN(0);
History misN(0);
History vecN(0);
History underN(0);
History lastFp(-1);
History hLWt(0);
History hLFp(0);
History hLGs(0);
History hLGe(0);
History hLCm(0);
History hLAg(0);
History ringOk(0);
History wTau(0);
History gapS(0);
History gapE(0);
History muteLeft(0);
History sAge(0);
History quietCnt(0);
History levelPk(0);
History teleAcc(0);
History frameNo(0);
History sleepNote(0);
History ringAge(0);
History gRun(0);
History alignRes(0);

//@@SECTION main
sr = max(samplerate, 1);

// ---- sample counter (modulo 2^22), vector position ----
sCc = sCnt;
sCnt = sCc + 1 >= 4194304 ? 0 : sCc + 1;
sVsz = vectorsize;
sVp = sCc - sVsz * floor(sCc / sVsz);
sVec = sVp < 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
sVend = sVp > sVsz - 1.5 ? 1 : 0;
ringAge = min(ringAge + 1, 4194304);

// ---- Size (the leader's; a follower ignores it) ----
nReq = cep_n(fftn);
nOld = nCur;
nChg = (nOld > 0.5 && nReq != nOld) ? 1 : 0;
nCur = nReq;
n = nReq;

// ---- control values, refreshed every 32 samples (and at once when n changes) ----
sCtl = sCtl + 1;
if (sCtl >= 32 || nChg > 0.5 || sBoot < 0.5) {
	sBoot = 1;
	sCtl = 0;
	selH = clip(floor(outsel + 0.5), 0, @@K@@);
	roleH = clip(floor(role + 0.5), -1, 2);
	serveH = clip(floor(serve + 0.5), 0, @@SERVEMAX@@);
	epH = floor(epoch + 0.5);
	mixH = clip(mixamt, 0, 1);
	sOwnH = selH > 0.5 ? pow(2, selH - 1) : pow(2, @@K@@);
	ownBit = floor(serveH / sOwnH);
	ownBit = ownBit - 2 * floor(ownBit / 2);
	eserveH = serveH > 0.5 ? (ownBit > 0.5 ? serveH : serveH + sOwnH) : sOwnH;
	for (c = 0; c <= @@K@@; c += 1) {
		fb2 = floor(eserveH / pow(2, c));
		fb2 = fb2 - 2 * floor(fb2 / 2);
		sFlag.poke(fb2, c);
	}
	//@hook ctl
}

// ---- roles: follow the leader's ring, or compute ----
sEpNew = epH != epSeen ? 1 : 0;
epSeen = epH;
if (sEpNew > 0.5) {
	fbk = 0;
	als = 0;
	noMatch = 0;
	staleN = 0;
	misN = 0;
	underN = 0;
}
sWantF = roleH > 1.5 ? 1 : 0;
sPend = roleH < -0.5 ? 1 : 0;
sFol = (sWantF > 0.5 && fbk < 0.5) ? 1 : 0;
sCmp = (sFol > 0.5 || sPend > 0.5) ? 0 : 1;
sStart = (sCmp > 0.5 && cmpH < 0.5) ? 1 : 0;
cmpH = sCmp;
sRest = (sStart > 0.5 || (nChg > 0.5 && sCmp > 0.5)) ? 1 : 0;

// ---- input level, silence sleep, fingerprint into the ring ----
inAbs = max(abs(in1), abs(in2));
quietCnt = inAbs > 0.00001 ? 0 : min(quietCnt + 1, 100000000);
levelPk = max(inAbs, levelPk * 0.9995);
awake = quietCnt < n ? 1 : 0;
sFp = in1 + 0.6180339887498949 * in2;
sBase = ss2_slot(sCc, @@RS@@, @@STRIDE@@, @@HDR@@);
poke(ring, sFp, sBase, 0);

// ---- follower: leader header (once per vector), freshness, alignment, verification ----
if (sFol > 0.5 && sVec > 0.5) {
	hLWt = peek(lead, 0, 0);
	hLFp = peek(lead, 1, 0);
	hLGs = peek(lead, 2, 0);
	hLGe = peek(lead, 3, 0);
	hLCm = peek(lead, 4, 0);
	hLAg = peek(lead, 9, 0);
	vecN = vecN + 1;
	if (hLFp != lastFp) {
		lastFp = hLFp;
		staleN = 0;
	} else {
		staleN = staleN + sVsz;
	}
	if (hLCm < 0.5 || staleN > 4096) {
		als = 0;
		if (staleN > 24000 || (hLCm < 0.5 && hLAg > 0.5 && staleN > 12000)) {
			fbk = 2;
		}
	} else if (als < 0.5) {
		if (hLAg > 2304 && ringAge > 2304) {
			alignRes = ss2_align(ring, lead, aw, sCc, hLFp, @@RS@@, @@STRIDE@@, @@HDR@@, 64, 1500, 2048);
			if (alignRes < 7999999) {
				dOff = alignRes;
				als = 1;
				misN = 0;
				noMatch = 0;
			} else if (alignRes > 8999999) {
				noMatch = noMatch + 1;
				if (noMatch >= 160) {
					fbk = 1;       // the input differs from the leader's (or is displaced by more than the search span)
				}
			}
		}
	} else {
		alignRes = ss2_verify(ring, lead, sCc, dOff, @@RS@@, @@STRIDE@@, @@HDR@@, 4, 1100);
		if (alignRes < -0.5) {
			misN = misN + 1;
			if (misN >= 2) {
				als = 0;
			}
		} else if (alignRes > 0.5) {
			misN = 0;
		}
	}
}
sUse = (sFol > 0.5 && als > 0.5) ? 1 : 0;

// ---- computing instance: the STFT pipeline, all served channels, output ring writes ----
sTele = 0;
wNew = wTau;
if (sCmp > 0.5) {
	fft_init(tab);
	stft_win(win, n);
	if (sRest > 0.5) {
		// a new pipeline: clear its state; the output ring gets a gap [gapS, gapE) that readers fade around
		ss2_clear(accD, @@ACCROWS@@, 4096);
		stt.poke(0, 2);
		sAge = 0;
		tau0 = sCc - (n - 1);
		tau0 = tau0 - 4194304 * floor(tau0 / 4194304);
		if (ringOk < 0.5) {
			wTau = tau0;
			wNew = tau0;
			gapS = tau0;
		} else {
			wOldS = wTau;
			dGap = ss2_wd(tau0, wOldS);
			if (dGap > 0.5) {
				ss2_zero(ring, wOldS, dGap, @@RS@@, @@STRIDE@@, @@HDR@@);
				wTau = tau0;
				wNew = tau0;
			}
			gapS = wOldS;
		}
		ringOk = 1;
		gapE = sCc + @@GAPHEAD@@ >= 4194304 ? sCc + @@GAPHEAD@@ - 4194304 : sCc + @@GAPHEAD@@;
		muteLeft = n + 128;
	}
	sRdy = ss_in(ringL, ringR, stt, in1, in2, n);
	if (sRdy > 0.5) {
		teleAcc = teleAcc + n * 0.25;
	}
	if (sRdy > 0.5 && teleAcc >= 1024) {
		sTele = awake > 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
		teleAcc = 0;
	}
	if (sRdy > 0.5 && awake < 0.5) {
		sAge = 0;
	}
	if (sRdy > 0.5 && awake > 0.5) {
		ss_frame(fx, ringL, ringR, stt, win, n);
		fft_run(fx, tab, n, 0);
		ss_mid(fx, ms, n);
		//@hook frame
		sAge = min(sAge + 1, 3);
		for (c = 0; c <= @@K@@; c += 1) {
			fl = sFlag.peek(c);
			if (fl > 0.5) {
				ss2_copy(fx, fy, n);
				ss_apply(fy, @@MKD@@, @@MKB@@ + c, n);
				fft_run(fy, tab, n, 1);
				ss2_ola(accD, 2 * c, stt, fy, win, n);
			}
		}
		if (sTele > 0.5) {
			//@hook tele
		}
	}
	// this sample's output (the pipeline emits the sample of input time sCc - (n - 1)); rows that are not served read as zeros
	tauE = sCc - (n - 1);
	tauE = tauE - 4194304 * floor(tauE / 4194304);
	sWr = 0;
	if (ringOk > 0.5) {
		dW = ss2_wd(tauE, wTau);
		sWr = dW > -0.5 ? 1 : 0;
	}
	sBase2 = ss2_slot(tauE, @@RS@@, @@STRIDE@@, @@HDR@@);
	for (c = 0; c <= @@K@@; c += 1) {
		eyl = ss2_out(accD, 2 * c, stt);
		eyr = ss2_out(accD, 2 * c + 1, stt);
		if (muteLeft > 0.5) {
			eyl = 0;
			eyr = 0;
		}
		if (sWr > 0.5) {
			poke(ring, eyl, sBase2 + 1 + 2 * c, 0);
			poke(ring, eyr, sBase2 + 2 + 2 * c, 0);
		}
	}
	if (sWr > 0.5) {
		wNew = wTau + 1 >= 4194304 ? 0 : wTau + 1;
		wTau = wNew;
	}
	if (muteLeft > 0.5) {
		muteLeft = muteLeft - 1;
	}
} else {
	ringOk = 0;
}

// ---- header of this instance's ring (read by followers), once per vector, after the vector's data ----
if (sVend > 0.5) {
	fpHw = sCc + 1 >= 4194304 ? 0 : sCc + 1;
	poke(ring, sCmp, 4, 0);
	poke(ring, ringOk > 0.5 ? wNew : 0, 0, 0);
	poke(ring, fpHw, 1, 0);
	poke(ring, gapS, 2, 0);
	poke(ring, gapE, 3, 0);
	poke(ring, sCmp > 0.5 ? eserveH : 0, 5, 0);
	poke(ring, n, 6, 0);
	poke(ring, @@VERSION@@, 7, 0);
	poke(ring, @@LAT@@, 8, 0);
	poke(ring, ringAge, 9, 0);
}

// ---- reader: this instance's output channel from the own ring (computing) or the leader's ring (aligned follower) ----
sDo = sUse > 0.5 ? dOff : 0;
sTr = sCc + sDo - @@LAT@@;
sTr = sTr - 4194304 * floor(sTr / 4194304);
gS = sUse > 0.5 ? hLGs : gapS;
gE = sUse > 0.5 ? hLGe : gapE;
wT = sUse > 0.5 ? hLWt : wTau;
dS = ss2_wd(gS, sTr);
dE = ss2_wd(sTr, gE);
dU = ss2_wd(wT, sTr);
gG = 1;
if (dS > 0.5) {
	gG = min(1, dS / 256);
} else if (dE < 0) {
	gG = 0;
} else {
	gG = min(1, dE / 512);
}
sOkR = 0;
if (sUse > 0.5) {
	sOkR = (dU > 64 && dU < @@RS@@ - 64) ? 1 : 0;
	if (sOkR < 0.5) {
		underN = underN + 1;
	} else {
		underN = max(underN - 0.01, 0);
	}
	if (underN > 2000) {
		fbk = 3;
	}
} else if (sCmp > 0.5 && ringOk > 0.5) {
	sOkR = dU > 0 ? 1 : 0;
}
gRun = gRun + ((sOkR > 0.5 ? 1 : 0) - gRun) * 0.004;
sBase3 = ss2_slot(sTr, @@RS@@, @@STRIDE@@, @@HDR@@);
sKrow = (sUse < 0.5 && sFlag.peek(@@K@@) > 0.5 && selH < 0.5) ? 1 : 0;
yl = 0;
yr = 0;
if (sOkR > 0.5) {
	if (selH > 0.5) {
		yl = ss2_rd(ring, lead, sUse, sBase3 + 1 + 2 * (selH - 1));
		yr = ss2_rd(ring, lead, sUse, sBase3 + 2 + 2 * (selH - 1));
	} else if (sKrow > 0.5) {
		yl = ss2_rd(ring, lead, sUse, sBase3 + 1 + 2 * @@K@@);
		yr = ss2_rd(ring, lead, sUse, sBase3 + 2 + 2 * @@K@@);
	} else {
		for (c = 0; c < @@K@@; c += 1) {
			yl += ss2_rd(ring, lead, sUse, sBase3 + 1 + 2 * c);
			yr += ss2_rd(ring, lead, sUse, sBase3 + 2 + 2 * c);
		}
	}
}
wetL = yl * gG * gRun;
wetR = yr * gG * gRun;

// ---- telemetry scalars: every 1024 samples for every instance (arrays come from the computing instance's hook) ----
sT1k = (sCc - 1024 * floor(sCc / 1024)) < 0.5 ? 1 : 0;
if (sTele > 0.5) {
	frameNo = wrap(frameNo + 1, 0, 102400);
	poke(scope, frameNo, @@SCB@@, 0);
}
if (sT1k > 0.5) {
	sLag = ss2_wd(hLFp, sCc + dOff);
	sLag = sUse > 0.5 ? sLag : 0;
	if (sCmp < 0.5) {
		frameNo = wrap(frameNo + 1, 0, 102400);
		poke(scope, frameNo, @@SCB@@, 0);
	}
	poke(scope, sr, @@SCB@@ + 1, 0);
	poke(scope, n, @@SCB@@ + 2, 0);
	poke(scope, awake, @@SCB@@ + 3, 0);
	poke(scope, levelPk, @@SCB@@ + 4, 0);
	poke(scope, @@LAT@@, @@SCB@@ + 6, 0);
	poke(scope, selH, @@SCB@@ + 7, 0);
	poke(scope, sCmp, @@SCB@@ + 8, 0);
	poke(scope, sFol, @@SCB@@ + 9, 0);
	poke(scope, als, @@SCB@@ + 10, 0);
	poke(scope, fbk, @@SCB@@ + 11, 0);
	poke(scope, sUse > 0.5 ? dOff : 0, @@SCB@@ + 12, 0);
	poke(scope, underN, @@SCB@@ + 13, 0);
	poke(scope, sLag, @@SCB@@ + 14, 0);
	poke(scope, eserveH, @@SCB@@ + 15, 0);
	poke(scope, roleH, @@SCB@@ + 16, 0);
	poke(scope, floor(sCc / 1024), @@SCB@@ + 17, 0);
}
if (awake < 0.5 && sleepNote < 0.5 && sCmp > 0.5) {
	ss2_zeroscope(scope, @@ZEROCNT@@);
	poke(scope, 0, @@SCB@@ + 3, 0);
	poke(scope, 0, @@SCB@@ + 4, 0);
	sleepNote = 1;
}
if (awake > 0.5) {
	sleepNote = 0;
}

// ---- Mix: out = mix * wet + (1 - mix) * dry / K (K chains sum in a rack), dry delayed like the wet ----
dryL.write(in1);
dryR.write(in2);
if (mixInit < 0.5) {
	mixInit = 1;
	mixS = mixH;
}
mixS = mixS + (mixH - mixS) * 0.002;
kShare = selH > 0.5 ? @@KSHARE@@ : 1;
ov1 = fixnan(fixdenorm(mixS * wetL + (1 - mixS) * kShare * dryL.read(@@LAT@@)));
ov2 = fixnan(fixdenorm(mixS * wetR + (1 - mixS) * kShare * dryR.read(@@LAT@@)));
// fixdenorm leaves 1e-38..1e-30 (decaying tails); flush that range too.
out1 = abs(ov1) < 1e-30 ? 0 : ov1;
out2 = abs(ov2) < 1e-30 ? 0 : ov2;
